WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:03.762
This is my first hackathon.
I have a friend who busks,

00:03.762 --> 00:05.342
and busking is guesswork.

00:06.350 --> 00:09.580
Foot traffic tells you
how many people walk past.

00:09.580 --> 00:13.403
It doesn't tell you who they
are, or what they'd stop for.

00:13.403 --> 00:14.063
Qloo does.

00:14.950 --> 00:18.191
Busk Map is an agent that
tells you where to busk,

00:18.191 --> 00:21.950
when, and what to play. Pick
an act, or describe your own.

00:22.850 --> 00:26.577
Then its agent, the Hive,
researches the city live,

00:26.577 --> 00:30.011
and you watch every step
in plain words: taste,

00:30.011 --> 00:33.445
venues, events, estimated
activity and weather.

00:34.350 --> 00:38.200
Qloo's heatmap shows where
your taste concentrates.

00:38.200 --> 00:44.164
Busk Map ranks real pitches, and keeps
the top three at least 250 metres apart.

00:45.050 --> 00:48.544
For each pitch, Qloo says
who the local crowd likes.

00:48.544 --> 00:52.979
Your set is ordered by how well
each artist lands with that crowd.

00:53.883 --> 00:58.027
Every plan also shows what a
plain AI picks with no data,

00:58.027 --> 01:00.208
so you can see what Qloo adds.

01:01.117 --> 01:04.456
Songs you should learn
come from your Repertoire.

01:04.456 --> 01:09.772
Qloo finds what your fans also love, and
the Hive never suggests a song twice.

01:10.683 --> 01:13.781
The Brain page shows
every kind of Qloo call,

01:13.781 --> 01:17.016
the data it returns, and
the feature it powers.

01:17.917 --> 01:21.052
And it's built for the street:
it works on your phone,

01:21.052 --> 01:21.865
with no login.

01:22.750 --> 01:25.655
Busk Map. Plan your busk,
and play the right pitch.
